# ArduCopter V4.7.2 failsafes for gate 1 (ADR-0007 section 3): each is
# switched on with the action its documentation gives as the usual one,
# because a default of "warn only" is not a response. No other parameter is
# set to make ArduCopter's response resemble ours. The battery thresholds
# (BATT_LOW_VOLT, BATT_CRT_VOLT) come from our core's own thresholds
# (oxide_bridge::faults::battery_failsafe_params), not from this file.
# The geofence is the scenario's own (FENCE_*), written by the runner.

# Radio lost (row "Radio lost"): 1 = return to launch.
FS_THR_ENABLE 1
# Estimator unhealthy, which is what a lost GPS becomes (row "Estimator
# unhealthy (GPS lost)"): 1 = land.
FS_EKF_ACTION 1
# Battery low (row "Battery low"): 2 = return to launch.
BATT_FS_LOW_ACT 2
# Battery critical (row "Battery critical"): 1 = land.
BATT_FS_CRT_ACT 1
# Ground station lost (row "Ground station lost"): 1 = return to launch.
FS_GCS_ENABLE 1
